{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3047","id":4554278175,"node_id":"PR_kwDOIZiOrM8AAAABD3TFHw","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3047","diff_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3047.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3047.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3047","number":3047,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve ordinary inode identity after standard descriptor reuse","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[hermit2, degraded-unresolved, gpt-6-astra, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\nWhen a file or pipe replaces descriptor 0, 1 or 2, Hermit must identify the replacement object. Previously, `fstat` assigned the fixed stdin/stdout/stderr identity from the descriptor number alone. This repair selects that existing rule only for descriptors carrying inherited-container-stream metadata and uses the ordinary inode pool for replacement objects across stat, fdinfo, maps and proc-fd links.\n\nThe KVM path also needs the landed Reverie proc-fd repair and its actual mount snapshot. Advance the coherent Reverie pin to `596b9adee8473dc0a7e62dce18580eead3d0c5c9` from https://github.com/rrnewton/reverie/pull/565 and validate captured mount rows before normalizing them. The unchanged descriptor-reuse and complete-stat-routes fixtures now complete on both ptrace and KVM. This moves KVM toward the owner's production parity goal while preserving the original closed-input regression assertions.\n\nTask: kvm-lane-to-full-determinism-and-parity\n\n## Determinism\n\nExisting descriptor resource metadata selects the existing inode rule. Opening a replacement file or pipe creates an ordinary object; `dup` shares its open-file metadata and pooled identity. No new allocator, scheduler order or source of time is introduced. Historical inherited-stream aliases above descriptor 2 retain their existing behavior.\n\nMount normalization uses the backend's completed namespace snapshot and requires the original captured rows and parent IDs to match before changing the configuration. Ambient capture failure, malformed rows, mismatched captured order, or nonempty uncaptured identity vectors are refused; valid absent provenance is captured. Existing strict parsing, ordered-subset checks and allocation rules remain intact.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nReusing a descriptor number does not preserve the closed object's identity. Duplicated descriptors of the same object must agree. The fixture checks replacement files and pipes at all three standard descriptor slots, surviving aliases, pathname and empty-path stat/statx, followed and no-follow proc-fd metadata, fdinfo, links and error controls.\n\nThe original closed-stdin `/bin/cat` assertions still require exit 1, empty stdout and a bad-file-descriptor error before the added descriptor-reuse control. The historical loader failure's complete causal path is not established by the narrower fixture results. Broader fdinfo normalization and retained-snapshot limitations remain separate.\n\n## Relationship to gVisor\n\nKVM continues to execute the shared Detcore tool through Reverie. The change repairs Linux descriptor handling and supplies the backend namespace to the existing Detcore normalization; it does not add a separate determinism engine.\n\n## Validation\n\nCandidate: `a88f948021a24c6a1ea808f868516c0691c8819a`, based on main `158a89f6217b25db9540237f9c1e256cdbaf785c`. Independent composition review verifies the complete tree and preserves the descriptor and mount commits from measured source `aa7ea4827b8328345e715d76518d7f2205e41110`. A separate test-only follow-up gives the backend fixture commands the existing owned temporary working directory; official validation still sets the guest working directory to `/test`. The following measurements remain attributed to aa7:\n\n- All 19 selected native methods passed: four new mount configuration controls, three strict-parser controls and twelve existing identity/procfs controls. Formatting, generated-DAG consistency and workspace/all-target Clippy with third-party backends and warnings denied passed.\n- Nextest inventory contains exactly 634 methods, the prior 630 plus the four new controls. Listing executed no tests. The generated DAG changes only the two corresponding expected unit counts; test selections and resource bounds remain unchanged.\n- With published Hermit binary SHA256 `a31abf5547e55c221b5a79fdff728ab2c4313882ace1a8473eac6890734a74fd`, the unchanged descriptor-reuse fixture passed once on ptrace (1.872 seconds) and once on KVM (1.825 seconds). The complete-stat-routes mode passed once natively (0.535 seconds), once on ptrace (1.954 seconds) and once on KVM (2.046 seconds). Times are wall time. Backend runs used INFO logging, strict mode, a minimal environment, fixed `/test`, unchanged assertions and 15 CPU / 30 wall second bounds. No retry, truncation, resource kill or leftover service occurred.\n\nThe official pinned-image 24-method KVM CLI node is pending. The earlier a9 launch stopped before tests because the admission check could not resolve that unpublished candidate through its default local checkout or GitHub. Publication resolved that lookup; the subsequent main update is preserved in the current candidate. The original cat assertion remains an outstanding validation obligation; all refused launches ran zero tests. The separate full Reverie library run remains **426 passed, 1 failed**, with reverse futex requeue returning 0 instead of 1 during fixture preparation; no measured base comparison or causal attribution is claimed. Failed attempts remain retained.\n\nThese checks do not establish a full-validation green result, within-backend strict-repeat determinism or canonical cross-backend parity. They do not change the historical 119-cell census.\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T03:26:53Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T07:30:29Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3047/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/3047/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/issues/3047/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rrnewton/hermit/statuses/a88f948021a24c6a1ea808f868516c0691c8819a","head":{"label":"rrnewton:codex/kvm-parity-recovery-20260916","ref":"codex/kvm-parity-recovery-20260916","sha":"a88f948021a24c6a1ea808f868516c0691c8819a","user":{"login":"rrnewton","id":274582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton","html_url":"https://github.com/rrnewton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrnewton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rrn